WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.904
With the right choice of new variables a complicated equation takes a very simple form,

2
00:00:05.904 --> 00:00:08.448
called the canonical form.

3
00:00:08.448 --> 00:00:16.056
In this part we write the characteristic equation and reduce a hyperbolic equation to canonical form step by step,

4
00:00:16.056 --> 00:00:19.214
finding its general solution.

5
00:00:19.464 --> 00:00:27.552
The characteristic equation is a d y squared minus two b d x d y plus c d x squared equals zero.

6
00:00:27.552 --> 00:00:30.264
Note the minus sign in the middle.

7
00:00:30.264 --> 00:00:38.304
If a is not zero, d y over d x equals b plus or minus the square root of the discriminant, divided by a.

8
00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:43.142
The integral curves of these ODEs are called characteristics.

9
00:00:43.392 --> 00:00:50.088
In the hyperbolic case there are two real characteristic families and, in suitable new coordinates,

10
00:00:50.088 --> 00:00:54.864
the canonical form reduces to u xi eta equals F.

11
00:00:54.864 --> 00:01:01.512
The parabolic case has one real family, while the elliptic case has no real characteristics.

12
00:01:01.512 --> 00:01:09.408
An important qualification is that the PDE type is preserved under smooth real coordinate changes with nonzero Jacobian.

13
00:01:09.408 --> 00:01:15.014
Degenerate or singular transformations are not covered by that statement.

14
00:01:15.264 --> 00:01:21.672
Example: u x x minus two u x y minus three u y y equals zero.

15
00:01:21.672 --> 00:01:26.016
a is one, b is minus one, c is minus three.

16
00:01:26.016 --> 00:01:32.270
The discriminant is one plus three, which is four, positive: hyperbolic.

17
00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:39.000
Characteristic equation: y prime squared plus two y prime minus three equals zero.

18
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.904
The roots are one and minus three.

19
00:01:41.904 --> 00:01:48.000
Integrating gives y minus x equals C one and y plus three x equals C two.

20
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:55.814
Take these as new variables: xi equals y minus x, and eta equals y plus three x.

21
00:01:56.064 --> 00:02:01.248
Compute the coefficients: A and C are zero and B is minus eight.

22
00:02:01.248 --> 00:02:08.880
The equation becomes minus sixteen u xi eta equals zero, that is u xi eta equals zero.

23
00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:18.230
The general solution is u equals f of y minus x plus g of y plus three x, with arbitrary functions f and g.

24
00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:24.576
The graph shows the two characteristics through the origin: y equals x with slope one,

25
00:02:24.576 --> 00:02:28.776
and y equals minus three x with slope minus three.

26
00:02:28.776 --> 00:02:33.456
The solution is carried along each family without changing shape.

27
00:02:33.456 --> 00:02:39.734
For the wave equation these lines are x plus or minus a t equals a constant.

28
00:02:39.984 --> 00:02:44.928
Now check: what are the characteristics of the wave equation on screen?

29
00:02:44.928 --> 00:02:49.070
Watch the speed a: it comes from a square root.
